root_cause.text:
Root cause:
The `cd321x_update_work` function in `drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c` fails to return early when `typec_register_partner` returns an error pointer, leading to a subsequent dereference of the invalid `tps->partner` pointer in `typec_partner_set_identity`.

Evidence:
The patch diff shows that when `IS_ERR(tps->partner)` is true, the code originally only logged a warning and continued execution:
```c
		tps->partner = typec_register_partner(tps->port, &desc);
-		if (IS_ERR(tps->partner))
-			dev_warn(tps->dev, "%s: failed to register partnet\n", __func__);
+		if (IS_ERR(tps->partner)) {
+			dev_warn(tps->dev, "%s: failed to register partner\n", __func__);
+			return;
+		}

 		if (desc.identity) {
 			typec_partner_set_identity(tps->partner);
```

